## 🧑🏾‍🏫 what this challenge teaches u
all gprs are divided in:
caller-saved regs -> regs that (conventionally) are not restored after a function has been called
rax, rcx, rdx, rsi, rdi, r8, r9, r10, r11

callee-saved regs -> regs that (conventionally) are restored after a function has been called
rbx, rbp, r12, r13, r14, r15

this means that if u call a function and u store important datas in caller-saved regs, u r not guarantee that when the funcion returns, u will get them back
thats why u have to use callee-saved regs or push those values in the stack

